Key safety notes first
- Do not send your full SSN over unsecured email or public chat. Use secure upload tools, an in‑person visit, or official website forms.  
- In communications you can safely reference only the last four digits (e.g., “SSN ending in 3456”) unless an official form specifically requests the full number.  
- Ask for mail delivery or in-person pickup rather than email of the card/verification, because agencies rarely transmit full SSNs by email.

Template: Formal letter (mail or to upload)
[Your full name]
[Your address]
