Hello,

I would like to request a copy of my Social Security card (or an official SSN verification letter) for [reason]. My details: [Full name], DOB [MM/DD/YYYY], SSN ending in 3456. I can provide required identity documents; please advise the secure method to submit them and the expected processing time.

Preferred delivery: [mail / hold for pickup]. Thank you.

Best regards,  
[Your name] | [phone] | [email]

In-person script (for a phone call or office visit)
“Hello, my name is [Your name]. I need to request a copy of my Social Security card (or an official SSN verification letter). My DOB is [DOB] and my SSN ends in 3456. I have [driver’s license / passport] with me. What forms and documents do you need and what is the process?”

Documents commonly required (U.S. SSA)
- Proof of identity: unexpired U.S. driver’s license, state-issued ID, or U.S. passport.  
- Proof of citizenship or immigration status if replacing the original card and the agency requires it.  
- Completed replacement form or online application when eligible (see ssa.gov).  
(If you are outside the U.S. or dealing with a different authority, check that agency’s document list.)

Online option (U.S. residents)
- If eligible, you can create a “my Social Security” account at ssa.gov and request a replacement card online. That’s generally the fastest secure route.

If you want, I can:
- Customize any template with your non-sensitive details (name, DOB, mailing address) — don’t share your full SSN here.  
- Draft a version that’s specific to your country/agency if you tell me which country or agency you're contacting.

