I can help — below are clear, safe ways to phrase a request to the Social Security Administration (SSA) or your issuing authority when you need a copy/verification of your SSN. I avoid repeating your full number here; if you want me to insert your last four digits into any template, confirm which four you want included.

Key points before you contact them
- What to ask for: “replacement Social Security card” (if you need the card) or an “SSN verification / SSA benefit verification letter” (if you only need proof of the number for an employer/agency).
- How to submit: use SSA’s official channels (online at ssa.gov if eligible, secure mail, or an in‑person visit to a local SSA office). Don’t send your full SSN over unsecured email or public messaging.
- Documents typically required: proof of identity (U.S. passport, state driver’s license, or state ID), proof of citizenship or immigration status (birth certificate, passport, or immigration documents), and proof of name change, if applicable. Originals or certified copies are usually required for mail/in‑person.
- Timing: processing times vary (often 10–14 business days for replacement cards once processed), but ask the office for the current estimate.

Formal letter/email template (for SSA or issuing authority)
- Subject: Request for Replacement Social Security Card / SSN Verification

Body:
To Whom It May Concern,

I am writing to request a replacement Social Security card / an official verification of my Social Security number. My information is:

- Full name: [First Middle Last]  
- Date of birth: [MM/DD/YYYY]  
- Last four digits of SSN: [####]  
- Current address: [Street, City, State, ZIP]  
- Phone: [###-###-####]  
- Email: [you@example.com]

Reason for request: [e.g., lost/stolen card; need verification for employer/agency]

Enclosed (or attached) are copies of the required identity documents:
- Proof of identity: [e.g., U.S. passport / state driver’s license]  
- Proof of citizenship or lawful status: [e.g., birth certificate / passport / I-551]  
- Proof of name change (if applicable): [e.g., marriage certificate / court order]

Please let me know if you need any additional documents or information and advise on the next steps. If you require my full Social Security number for processing, please advise a secure method for providing it (or I can provide it in person at a local SSA office).

Thank you for your assistance.

Sincerely,  
[Your full name]  
[Signature if mailing]  
[Mailing address]  
[Phone and email]

Short phone script
Hello — my name is [Name]. I need to request a replacement Social Security card / an official SSN verification letter. My date of birth is [DOB] and the last four digits of my SSN are [####]. What is the safest way to provide my full SSN and the required identity documents, and what should I bring or mail to complete this request?

Security note to include when emailing
If you must email, say you will not include the full SSN in the message and ask for a secure portal or instructions to submit it safely. Example: “For security, I will not send my full SSN by unsecured email. Please confirm a secure method for submitting my full SSN and originals/certified copies of my identity documents.”

Want me to:
- Insert your last four digits into one of the templates? (Confirm which four to use.)  
- Draft a shorter version tailored to an employer or a specific agency?  
- Search for the local SSA office mailing address and hours?

